1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:02,160
GTA 6 is finally out.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,010
And it has one big problem.

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,355
It runs at thirty frames per second.

4
00:00:06,355 --> 00:00:07,655
On every console.

5
00:00:07,693 --> 00:00:09,580
Even the PS5 Pro.

6
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,775
There's no sixty FPS mode.

7
00:00:11,812 --> 00:00:13,000
Not even forty.

8
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:16,045
And Digital Foundry found the base PS5

9
00:00:16,045 --> 00:00:17,595
can dip into the low twenties in

10
00:00:17,595 --> 00:00:18,745
heavy action.

11
00:00:18,965 --> 00:00:20,990
The reason? The CPU.

12
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:22,165
There's so much traffic,

13
00:00:22,165 --> 00:00:23,128
crowds and physics,

14
00:00:23,128 --> 00:00:24,727
that a faster mode would mean cutting

15
00:00:24,727 --> 00:00:25,340
them.

16
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,685
But Digital Foundry still calls it the

17
00:00:27,685 --> 00:00:30,435
most visually striking game of the generation.

18
00:00:30,705 --> 00:00:31,705
So be honest.

19
00:00:31,705 --> 00:00:33,180
Would you trade the crowds for sixty

20
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:35,280
FPS? Yes or no?

